{"skill":{"slug":"agent-task-tracker","displayName":"Task Tracker"},"version":{"version":"1.1.0","createdAt":1771441209751,"changelog":"Add 50-line/2KB size limit, completed task compression to one-line summaries, auto-prune >3 days","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1920,"sha256":"a97d321b21aa7fa3cad6612ef9015caec1a5556fe4328f90f19e49645fc778ed","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1973,"sha256":"e5ddc080efe466fb4b893e647a8db28f4427a2ebb46fa281299a9cdf02c4400b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789072857272,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5aa45af30aef227ad2e6be58ae33f7d0521ca29e914730579e6545b74e18dff8","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5aa45af30aef227ad2e6be58ae33f7d0521ca29e914730579e6545b74e18dff8","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: agent-task-tracker\nVersion: 1.1.0\n\nThe skill bundle defines a task tracking mechanism for an AI agent, instructing it to maintain a state file (`memory/tasks.md`) to record details about its ongoing and completed tasks, including background processes and their associated commands. All instructions in `SKILL.md` are aligned with the stated purpose of proactive task state management and do not contain any indicators of malicious intent, data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, or prompt injection designed to subvert the agent for harmful purposes.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779165253111},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":89,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789072857272},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a task tracker, but it automatically records task details and operational metadata across sessions without enough scoping or redaction guidance.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Recording full commands, server names, session IDs, PIDs, notes, results, and links is broader than necessary for many task-tracking uses and can capture sensitive operational context.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact contains only a Markdown skill file and no bundled executable code, dependency installer, network retrieval, or privilege escalation mechanism.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill says it triggers automatically for every task lifecycle event and requires write-first behavior before user updates, which gives it broad influence over unrelated tasks.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill persistently writes to memory/tasks.md, reads it on session start, and lacks clear consent, opt-out, redaction, access-control, or sensitive-task handling instructions.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is coherent: maintain a persistent task state file so work can resume after resets or compaction.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with the agent maintaining a persistent task file for nearly all work. Avoid using it around secrets, private commands, authenticated links, sensitive server names, or confidential task outputs unless the skill is changed to minimize and redact stored data.","findings":"[SQP-1] unexpected: Automatic activation is disclosed, but applying it to every task and requiring writes before user updates is materially overbroad for a task tracker.\n[E4] unexpected: The artifact does not transmit data externally, so this is not validated as exfiltration, but it does instruct durable storage of raw session, server, PID, command, result, and link metadata that may be sensitive.\n[SSD-3] expected: Cross-session persistence is central to the stated purpose, but the artifact does not sufficiently limit what gets stored or how sensitive entries are avoided.\n[SQP-2] expected: The state file is explicitly documented and retention is partially bounded by pruning guidance, but user control and redaction expectations are under-specified.\n[SQP-3] expected: Fixed Chinese status labels are a usability concern, not a security concern, and do not drive the verdict.\n[T01] unexpected: The static finding is supported in part: the artifact globally changes workflow by requiring automatic task-state reads and writes across sessions.\n[T09] unexpected: The static finding is supported in part: the artifact directs plaintext retention of operational metadata without redaction or consent controls.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789072857272}}}}}